{"format":1,"seq":592,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm weighing whether to always add a marker like `PI_ACTION_RUNNING: \"true\"` to the tool environment versus placing it elsewhere, since always including it would affect the existing tests that check exact equality.\n\nThen I realize the real issue: my nested run went through pit's in-process shell, which uses the actual process environment, not a subprocess's. So the marker needs to live in `process.env` itself, set once at the start of `index.ts` before anything spawns, so that both pit's in-process execution and any spawned bash processes (which inherit process env plus `shellEnv`) will see it. I'm sketching a small helper module to set and check this environment flag at run startup.\n\nI also want `push.ts` to check this flag defensively — the outer push step runs as its own process with a clean env, so it won't trip the guard, but if a nested agent run tries to invoke `push.ts` directly, that could race against the outer push. I'll have push.ts only check, not claim, the flag.\n\nFor wiring this into `run()`, I'm worried about test isolation: if `run()` mutates `deps.env ?? process.env` directly, and tests don't always pass a fresh `deps.env`, I could end up stamping `process.env` itself and leaking state across test runs in the same worker. Safer to put the claiming logic only in `index.ts` (the actual entrypoint) rather than inside `run()`, and keep it unit-tested separately — I should check `entrypoints.test.ts` to see what it already covers before deciding.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since pit's shell.execFile inherits pi-action's own process.env rather than the bash tool env, the marker needs to be set at pi-action startup so child processes inherit it. I'll check how the entry points are tested next.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01CAv6SEHagrdA68VjwphTdR","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read entrypoints.test.ts\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const r = await exec(`cat src/entrypoints.test.ts | head -120; cat knip.json; grep -n \"exclude\\\\|include\" vitest.config.ts`, {});\n  return r.stdout;\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1435,"cacheRead":119748,"cacheWrite":2582,"totalTokens":123767,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1278},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794610305336,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_vkiny4hoglpybv7rspoqbfnkadt2skwebz3wi456tecxzxxaffja","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":20134,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":203,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":202}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":202,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"waiting","checkpoint":{"phase":"tools","assistant":203,"tools":[204],"pending":[]},"on":[204],"policy":"allSettled"},"startedAt":1794610305306}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":204,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.tool","version":3,"input":{"kind":"model","assistant":203,"callId":"toolu_bdrk_01CAv6SEHagrdA68VjwphTdR"},"owner":202,"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"pending","checkpoint":{"phase":"call"}}}},{"type":"document.change","id":2,"content":{"version":3,"kind":"base","value":{"run":{"taskId":202,"inputs":[176],"turns":7,"first":175},"tools":[{"callId":"toolu_bdrk_01CAv6SEHagrdA68VjwphTdR","name":"typescript","taskId":204,"status":"pending"}]}}},{"type":"document.change","id":4,"content":{"version":1,"kind":"base","value":{"models":{"nvidia/aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5":{"input":94,"output":32950,"cacheRead":3018724,"cacheWrite":302706,"totalTokens":3354474,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"t